# Rank 1975 / CVE-2024-31996 (GHSA-hf43-47q4-fhq5, CWE-94, CWE-95): the
# XWiki escaping tool's `html()` inherits Velocity Tools' HTML-entity
# escaping, which covers `& < > " '` and nothing else
# (xwiki-commons-core/xwiki-commons-velocity/src/main/java/org/xwiki/velocity/tools/EscapeTool.java
# at fix parent b94142e2^):
#
#     public class EscapeTool extends org.apache.velocity.tools.generic.EscapeTool
#     {
#         @Override
#         public String xml(Object content) { ... }   // overridden
#         // no html() override: inherits escapeHtml4, entity-escaping only
#     }
#
# XWiki wiki syntax treats `{{ ... }}` as a macro. A template that answers
# with `$escapetool.html($request.place)` therefore passes the braces
# through, and the advisory's PoC ships `{{/html}}{{velocity}}#evaluate(
# $request.eval)` in the `place` parameter of `Panels.PanelLayoutUpdate`,
# closing the enclosing HTML macro and evaluating attacker Velocity on the
# server. Fix b94142e2 overrides `html()` with a translator that also maps
# `{` to `&lcub;` and `}` to `&rcub;` -- the row's commit is the master
# original and the advisory's other two commits (b080516, ed7ff51) are its
# cherry-picks to the release branches, so the row is correct and the
# remediation is present at the fixed revision. .
#
# ATTENTION, analysis gap, with an empty measurable set on the assigned tree.
# Measured exhaustively at the vulnerable revision:
#   - `grep -rn escapetool` over the whole checkout: 2 hits, the class's own
#     `DEFAULT_KEY` constant and a `${escapetool.h}` literal in its test.
#     Zero call sites of `html()` anywhere -- no `.vm`, no `.xml`, no Java.
#   - 3 `.vm` files exist (license/XAR boilerplate), none call escapetool;
#     the 4 xwikidoc XML fixtures that pass the config scope gate contain
#     no escapetool either.
#   - `vyql match` on EscapeTool.java labels nothing: no source, no sink,
#     one unrelated `encodedURL.replaceAll` CharFilter at line 272.
#   - bounded scan of the change-carrying subtree
#     (xwiki-commons-core/xwiki-commons-velocity, java:54 config:1
#     textpattern:54): 7 findings, all unrelated (2 WeakRandomValue in a
#     test, 1 ResourceHandle in NIOTool, 1 CleartextChannel in a test URL).
#   - `grep -rl escapetool.html` across every rank clone under /tmp/cve-work
#     at the time of review: 0 hits. The only tree that carries the shape is
#     xwiki-platform, whose sibling rank owns it.
# So no A/B revision pair and no collateral baseline exist here.
#
# Why nothing is shipped for the shape either:
#   - the Java side has no node to bind. At the parent there is no `html()`
#     method in the file at all, so a discriminating binding must key on the
#     *absence of an override* in a subclass of
#     `org.apache.velocity.tools.generic.EscapeTool`. That is the fixing
#     commit's own layout, and velocity-tools' documentation says nothing
#     that would lead anyone to write it: the genericity test fails, and
#     exactly one such class exists in the world.
#   - the template side is line-regex extraction, not nodes. The
#     `xwiki_velocity` config scope (bindings/config/m2b6375a9.vyql) emits
#     one source (`template.xwiki_velocity.input` ->
#     core.UserControlledData), one state-change sink and one CSRF check; it
#     has no escape notion and no render sink. `vyql graph` on the PoC
#     template below shows the whole document collapsing to a Const and an
#     Arg flowing into that single source call -- the `$escapetool.html()`
#     wrapper is text inside a matched line, not a node, so "escaped for
#     HTML" and "escaped for wiki syntax" are indistinguishable in the IR.
#     Representing them needs a new extraction fact (an escape call between
#     the request read and the render), which is a dataflow relation, not a
#     missing switch case. Judged not mechanical.
#   - `.vm` files are not analysed by any frontend ("no supported source
#     found" on a probe .vm holding `$escapetool.html($!request.x)`), so the
#     artifact type where the shape lives is outside the scope that does
#     exist.
#
# Kinship, for coordination with the xwiki-platform sibling rank: this is the
# same "output encoding sufficient for one parser and not the receiving one"
# family as code.JavaScriptTemplateHtmlEscapeMismatch (VYQL-INJ-171) and
# code.ErbHrefUrlHtmlEscapeOnly, and it must not become a third per-shape
# sibling. The vocabulary the family needs on the platform tree is one pair,
# measured together there: `$escapetool.html` bound as a core.HtmlEscape
# control (documentation-answerable -- the override's own javadoc is "Escapes
# the HTML special characters ... using HTML entities") beside a wiki-render
# sink, so the rule asks whether the escape covers the parser that reads the
# value. Landing the HtmlEscape half alone would be unmeasurable on a tree
# with no call sites and would suppress the very finding the sink half is
# meant to raise, so it belongs with the sink, not before it.
#
# verify_current_expected: attention-analysis-gap, all four tests rejected.
# The first two are the vulnerable and patched library forms; the third and
# fourth are the template pair, differing only in the escape call.
# When a wiki-render sink and an escape control land for this scope, the
# third test must flip to expect VYQL-INJ-004 and the fourth must stay
# reject -- they are the minimal pair, identical except for which escape
# wraps the value.

test "rank1975: the escaping tool inherits entity-only HTML escaping, braces unescaped"
  lang java
  file EscapeTool.java
  reject VYQL-INJ-004
  code
  ```
  package org.xwiki.velocity.tools;

  import java.util.Objects;
  import org.xwiki.xml.XMLUtils;

  public class EscapeTool extends org.apache.velocity.tools.generic.EscapeTool
  {
      public static final String DEFAULT_KEY = "escapetool";

      public EscapeTool()
      {
          setKey(DEFAULT_KEY);
      }

      @Override
      public String xml(Object content)
      {
          return XMLUtils.escape(Objects.toString(content, null));
      }
  }
  ```

test "rank1975: the patched tool escapes the braces the wiki parser reads"
  lang java
  file EscapeToolFixed.java
  reject VYQL-INJ-004
  code
  ```
  package org.xwiki.velocity.tools;

  import java.util.Map;
  import org.apache.commons.text.StringEscapeUtils;
  import org.apache.commons.text.translate.CharSequenceTranslator;
  import org.apache.commons.text.translate.LookupTranslator;

  public class EscapeTool extends org.apache.velocity.tools.generic.EscapeTool
  {
      public static final String DEFAULT_KEY = "escapetool";

      private static final CharSequenceTranslator XWIKI_ESCAPE_HTML4 = StringEscapeUtils.ESCAPE_HTML4.with(
          new LookupTranslator(Map.ofEntries(
              Map.entry("{", "&lcub;"),
              Map.entry("}", "&rcub;")
          ))
      );

      @Override
      public String html(Object content)
      {
          if (content == null) {
              return null;
          }
          return XWIKI_ESCAPE_HTML4.translate(String.valueOf(content));
      }
  }
  ```

test "rank1975: a request parameter escaped for HTML only still reaches the render"
  lang config
  file PanelLayoutUpdate.xml
  reject VYQL-INJ-004
  code
  ```
  <xwikidoc>
    <web>Panels</web>
    <name>PanelLayoutUpdate</name>
    <content><![CDATA[
  #set ($layout = "$request.place")
  $response.getWriter().print("$escapetool.html($layout)")
    ]]></content>
  </xwikidoc>
  ```

